From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <chrisbreuer93@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:15:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] sql: a query can be waited for without the event loop

query.wait(ms), query.executeSync(ms) and sql.reserveSync(ms) block the
calling thread on the socket of the one connection that has the answer,
and handle exactly what arrives on it. The loop does not turn, so nothing
else of the program runs in the middle of the caller's statement.

- usockets: us_socket_pump / us_connecting_socket_pump wait on one file
  descriptor and dispatch it as a tick would, TLS and connect included.
- PostgresSQLConnection and MySQLConnection get pump(ms).
- A name looked up for a SQL connection is resolved on the thread pool,
  whose answer the pump can see without a tick.
